# where the map is looking: "<lat>,<lon>,<zoom>". Where you are on the map is a
# fact about this phone and this hand, not about what you own — device-scoped,
# exactly as /browse's `view` and `open` are, and a device-scoped write queues
# no op. It survives an update because /patch/world-along carries the world
# across a hot swap and /world-cache brings it back on a reload, which is what
# makes "land where you were" true of both.
#
# Bridged, because the page half is the only half that can answer it: Leaflet
# is made there and asked for its view there.
map_view: String = String::new() (device, last-write, own) js:map_view
